{%- comment -%}
The email address as a link, without ever writing it into the page. The two
halves go out reversed and with no "@", and _js/email.js only puts them
together when the link is clicked, so the address is in neither the source nor
the live page for a scraper to find. The link reads `text` (default "email
me"), never the address; without JavaScript it goes nowhere.

Never print the halves as readable text here, not even as "name (at) domain
(dot) com": scrapers decode that routinely.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign email_user_reversed = site.email_user | split: "" | reverse | join: "" -%}
{%- assign email_domain_reversed = site.email_domain | split: "" | reverse | join: "" -%}
<a href="#" data-email-user="{{ email_user_reversed }}" data-email-domain="{{ email_domain_reversed }}">{{ include.text | default: "email me" }}</a>
